---@field thumbnailUrl? string Output only. The thumbnail URL for showing a preview of the given photo.
---@field uploadReference? gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.UploadRef Input only. Required when creating a photo. Input only. The resource URL where the photo bytes are uploaded to.
---@field photoId? gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.PhotoId Required. Output only. Required when updating a photo. Output only when creating a photo. Identifier for the photo, which is unique among all photos in Google.
---@field mapsPublishStatus? gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.PhotoMapsPublishStatusEnum|string Output only. Status in Google Maps, whether this photo was published or rejected.
---@field viewCount? string Output only. View count of the photo.
---@field shareLink? string Output only. The share link for the photo.
---@field pose? gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.Pose Optional. Pose of the photo.
---@field captureTime? string Optional. Absolute time when the photo was captured. When the photo has no exif timestamp, this is used to set a timestamp in the photo metadata.
---@field connections? gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.ConnectionList Optional. Connections to other photos. A connection represents the link from this photo to another photo.
---@field id string A unique identifier for a photo.
---@field updateMask? string Required. Mask that identifies fields on the photo metadata to update. If not present, the old Photo metadata is entirely replaced with the new Photo metadata in this request. The update fails if invalid fields are specified. Multiple fields can be specified in a comma-delimited list. The following fields are valid: * `pose.heading` * `pose.lat_lng_pair` * `pose.pitch` * `pose.roll` * `pose.level` * `pose.altitude` * `connections` * `places` > Note: When updateMask contains repeated fields, the entire set of repeated values get replaced with the new contents. For example, if updateMask contains `connections` and `UpdatePhotoRequest.photo.connections` is empty, all connections are removed.

---Upload reference for media files.
---@class gcp.streetviewpublish_v1.UploadRef
---@field uploadUrl? string An upload reference should be unique for each user. It follows the form: "https://streetviewpublish.googleapis.com/media/user/{account_id}/photo/{upload_reference}"

